nd inspired by the artistry, rituals and craftsmanship of The Royal Ballet.</p>","productionPageUrl":null,"slug":"youre-worth-it-afternoon-tea-and-tour","performances":[{"date":"2026-11-30T12:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-11-30T14:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-12T12:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-12T14:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-15T12:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-15T14:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-17T12:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-17T14:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-18T12:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-18T14:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-20T12:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"},{"date":"2026-12-20T14:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"guided-tour"}],"isCancelled":false,"ctaBehaviour":null,"cinemaBroadcastLink":{"validUntil":null,"url":"/cinemas/production/78897/findcinema"},"startTime":null,"endTime":null,"isHiddenFromTicketsAndEvents":false,"helpInformation":null,"tags":["927","1153"],"bookingSeasons":["1001"],"locations":["0"],"performanceTimes":[],"onSaleDates":["cae0a42192edd644d0823025d9ae185e0157a769"],"runs":["78897"],"festival":null},{"id":"74615","sourceType":"single-production-page","title":"Götterdämmerung","imageTray":{"desktopPath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adzDYJ1ZCF7ETIa6_GOTTERDAMMERUNG_RBO_0120FinalFinal_WEB.jpg?auto=format,compress&rect=0,67,4500,3375&w=1280&h=960","mobilePath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adzDYJ1ZCF7ETIa6_GOTTERDAMMERUNG_RBO_0120FinalFinal_WEB.jpg?auto=format,compress&rect=0,67,4500,3375&w=1280&h=960","thumbPath":null,"altText":"An elderly woman representing Erda in Barrie Kosky’s Götterdämmerung is at the centre of the frame. The woman’s expression is somber, she has pale skin and grey hair and is seen through a swirling, surreal, tunnel-like vortex. The scene is distorted as if viewed through spinning glass, with streaks of light, sparks, and warm glowing fragments spiralling around her.","caption":null},"imageResult":{"desktopPath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adzDYJ1ZCF7ETIa6_GOTTERDAMMERUNG_RBO_0120FinalFinal_WEB.jpg?auto=format,compress&rect=0,67,4500,3375&w=960&h=720","mobilePath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adzDYJ1ZCF7ETIa6_GOTTERDAMMERUNG_RBO_0120FinalFinal_WEB.jpg?auto=format,compress&rect=0,67,4500,3375&w=960&h=720","thumbPath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adzDYJ1ZCF7ETIa6_GOTTERDAMMERUNG_RBO_0120FinalFinal_WEB.jpg?auto=format,compress&rect=0,67,4500,3375&w=960&h=720","altText":"An elderly woman representing Erda in Barrie Kosky’s Götterdämmerung is at the centre of the frame. The woman’s expression is somber, she has pale skin and grey hair and is seen through a swirling, surreal, tunnel-like vortex. The scene is distorted as if viewed through spinning glass, with streaks of light, sparks, and warm glowing fragments spiralling around her.","caption":null},"dateFieldOverride":null,"description":"<p>Director Barrie Kosky situates this rich apocalyptic drama in a contemporary world of dream-like turmoil. A stellar cast, together with the full forces of the Orchestra of the Royal Opera House and Royal Opera Chorus, bring opera’s greatest journey to its shattering end.</p>","carouselDescription":"<p>The long-awaited finale of Wagner’s epic <em>Ring </em>cycle.</p>","productionPageUrl":"/production/gotterdammerung-barrie-kosky","slug":"gotterdammerung-barrie-kosky","performances":[{"date":"2027-01-21T16:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-01-24T14:30:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-01-27T16:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-01-30T16:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-02-03T16:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-02-07T14:30:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"}],"isCancelled":false,"ctaBehaviour":null,"cinemaBroadcastLink":{"validUntil":null,"url":null},"startTime":"2027-01-21T16:00:00+00:00","endTime":"2027-02-07T14:30:00+00:00","isHiddenFromTicketsAndEvents":false,"helpInformation":null,"tags":["921","1132","1349","585","923"],"bookingSeasons":["1002"],"locations":["2"],"performanceTimes":["936","935"],"onSaleDates":["56acd2c71f4dd81e38737e29bf5e42d9b801b016","89c4fc939ddc25844651aeb528c63c4ef361890f","0558db9dbbbc1a516844d831f451d86397daa44e","4dea8cdd62d70185e3dc2feac037ff9c74e5a36e","4c636a8472121d512d4893830bc48b0d59ee0065","076d9e4636d8c0a604c62daf5f87e02472b4c54d","2f8c1e30683833b6d172dd5f2a643dc2a07c3ec6","727ac4dda2a8242d2100221df9dfcfca7629646a"],"runs":[],"festival":null},{"id":"75408","sourceType":"single-production-page","title":"Good Sometimes Queen","imageTray":{"desktopPath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adeUpZ1ZCF7ETBlh_GSQ_HERO_CopyrightMilesAldridge.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C151%2C3820%2C2865&w=1280&h=960","mobilePath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adeUpZ1ZCF7ETBlh_GSQ_HERO_CopyrightMilesAldridge.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C151%2C3820%2C2865&w=1280&h=960","thumbPath":null,"altText":"Close-up side profile of a young woman with pale skin and red hair styled in a loose updo, set against a warm red textured background. Soft lighting highlights her cheekbone and eye as she gazes forward with a calm, neutral expression.","caption":null},"imageResult":{"desktopPath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adeUpZ1ZCF7ETBlh_GSQ_HERO_CopyrightMilesAldridge.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C184%2C3820%2C2865&w=960&h=720","mobilePath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adeUpZ1ZCF7ETBlh_GSQ_HERO_CopyrightMilesAldridge.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C184%2C3820%2C2865&w=960&h=720","thumbPath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adeUpZ1ZCF7ETBlh_GSQ_HERO_CopyrightMilesAldridge.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C184%2C3820%2C2865&w=960&h=720","altText":"Close-up side profile of a young woman with pale skin and red hair styled in a loose updo, set against a warm red textured background. Soft lighting highlights her cheekbone and eye as she gazes forward with a calm, neutral expression.","caption":null},"dateFieldOverride":null,"description":"<p>Ola Ince directs a new staging of two dramatic song cycles drawn from Elizabethan sources by Brett Dean. Lotte Betts-Dean and Jennifer France star in this new work of theatre exploring the fates of Mary, Queen of Scots and Shakespeare’s Ophelia, alongside the Doric String Quartet.</p>","carouselDescription":"<p>Two Elizabethan heroines. Two extraordinary works for the female voice by Brett Dean.</p>","productionPageUrl":"/production/good-sometimes-queen-ola-ince","slug":"good-sometimes-queen-ola-ince","performances":[{"date":"2027-01-23T19:45:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-01-24T14:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-01-25T19:45:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-01-27T19:45:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-01-28T19:45:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-01-29T19:45:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"}],"isCancelled":false,"ctaBehaviour":null,"cinemaBroadcastLink":{"validUntil":null,"url":null},"startTime":"2027-01-23T19:45:00+00:00","endTime":"2027-01-29T19:45:00+00:00","isHiddenFromTicketsAndEvents":false,"helpInformation":null,"tags":["606","921","1132","1349","312","934","1063","1064"],"bookingSeasons":["1001"],"locations":["73"],"performanceTimes":["936","935"],"onSaleDates":["1000ad5d978cdf1d2d9ed35a98915f049d5d5fcf","0558db9dbbbc1a516844d831f451d86397daa44e","5bfadc563bf9dfdf372cb06d772d287200e9a0b2","aa2d1537623290d7573a8dcca7caa5ef2d7c6b78","3a0bc3ec709efed904801f5433e3fb31029a519e","d79204d0ef8c691f2403c3ef25c74e58b557bc25","e2aca631972f28b09d3ac4440