 holding a bouquet of orange flowers that obscures their face. The person wears a muted blue top and a flowing orange skirt, with soft, moody lighting and a dreamy, slightly blurred effect.","caption":null},"imageResult":{"desktopPath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adeRpJ1ZCF7ETBjP_LesBoreades_stills_334314_nikolay.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C0%2C4096%2C3072&w=960&h=720","mobilePath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adeRpJ1ZCF7ETBjP_LesBoreades_stills_334314_nikolay.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C0%2C4096%2C3072&w=960&h=720","thumbPath":"https://images.prismic.io/royal-opera-house/adeRpJ1ZCF7ETBjP_LesBoreades_stills_334314_nikolay.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C0%2C4096%2C3072&w=960&h=720","altText":"A stylized, grainy photograph of a person sitting against a blue-toned background, holding a bouquet of orange flowers that obscures their face. The person wears a muted blue top and a flowing orange skirt, with soft, moody lighting and a dreamy, slightly blurred effect.","caption":null},"dateFieldOverride":null,"description":"<p>A defiant queen and meddlesome gods. R.B. Schlather directs a new production of Rameau’s most brilliant opera – the first work by the French composer to be performed at Covent Garden by The Royal Opera. Camille Delaforge conducts a stellar cast, bringing this rarely-performed Baroque gem to sparkling life. </p>","carouselDescription":"<p>Can love conquer all when Greek gods are involved? The Royal Opera&#39;s first performance of a work by Rameau at Covent Garden.</p>","productionPageUrl":"/production/les-boreades-rb-schlather","slug":"les-boreades-rb-schlather","performances":[{"date":"2027-03-04T19:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-03-05T19:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-03-07T14:00:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-03-08T19:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"},{"date":"2027-03-10T19:15:00+00:00","performanceType":"standard"